{
  "name": "47 · Lead Researcher (Kaamchor AI · MAP 3.0)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 47 · Lead Researcher\nBefore a sales call, paste the company's website in a form → AI reads the site and emails you a **one-page brief**: what they do, who they sell to, size, likely needs, talking points, a ready opener and a fit score. Saved in **Lead research**.\n\n**Setup (10 min)**\n1. Gmail nodes: add a **Gmail OAuth2** credential. Replace YOUR_OWNER_EMAIL.\n2. Google Sheets nodes: add a **Google Sheets OAuth2** credential and paste your sheet link in place of YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_URL. Tab **Lead research**: Date, Company, Website, Fit score, What they do, Needs, Opener.\n3. AI model node: add an **Anthropic** credential (or swap the model node for OpenAI / Gemini).\n\nOpen the form from the trigger's Production URL. Edit what you sell in the prompt.",
        "height": 532,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "9c4e7185-68a9-486b-9e42-ca28bf327f38",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -480,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "formTitle": "Research a lead",
        "formDescription": "Paste a company's website. A one-page brief comes to your email in about a minute.",
        "formFields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "fieldLabel": "Company name",
              "requiredField": true
            },
            {
              "fieldLabel": "Website",
              "placeholder": "https://...",
              "requiredField": true
            },
            {
              "fieldLabel": "What do you want to sell them?"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "1075b0a0-b38c-477f-82d3-630be01f34ae",
      "name": "Research form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $json.Website }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true,
              "responseFormat": "text"
            }
          },
          "timeout": 20000
        }
      },
      "id": "cfc19a46-2a31-4782-9aac-d9eef0d0cbf3",
      "name": "Open their website",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const clean = h => String(h || '').replace(/<script[\\s\\S]*?<\\/script>|<style[\\s\\S]*?<\\/style>|<noscript[\\s\\S]*?<\\/noscript>/gi, ' ')\n  .replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/&nbsp;/g, ' ').replace(/&amp;/g, '&').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\nconst f = $('Research form').item.json;\nreturn { json: { company: f['Company name'], website: f.Website, offer: f['What do you want to sell them?'] || 'our services', text: clean($json.data).slice(0, 8000) } };",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      },
      "id": "d297cbbc-b04b-4ebc-9a79-fe2c3fe84869",
      "name": "Clean text",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You research a sales lead for YOUR BUSINESS NAME, which sells: {{ $json.offer }}.\nCompany: {{ $json.company }} ({{ $json.website }})\nTheir website text:\n{{ $json.text }}\n\nReturn: what_they_do (2 lines), who_they_sell_to, size_signals (branches, team, years, clients mentioned; 'not stated' if none), likely_needs (3 bullets linked to what we sell), talking_points (3 bullets), opener (a 3-line first WhatsApp/LinkedIn message, friendly, no hard sell, no fake compliments), fit_score 1-10 with one-line reason. Use only the website text; never invent clients, numbers or people.",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
      "id": "18410be2-68a6-4d74-aef2-30d0baee3784",
      "name": "AI writes lead brief",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [
        720,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.3
        }
      },
      "id": "4dd0aeee-d930-4315-9991-bae1297e2bee",
      "name": "AI model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        660,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\n  \"what_they_do\": \"...\",\n  \"who_they_sell_to\": \"...\",\n  \"size_signals\": \"...\",\n  \"likely_needs\": [\n    \"...\"\n  ],\n  \"talking_points\": [\n    \"...\"\n  ],\n  \"opener\": \"Hello ...\",\n  \"fit_score\": 7,\n  \"fit_reason\": \"...\"\n}"
      },
      "id": "4eb7860c-35ec-43d3-8b72-d0f85cc2fb28",
      "name": "JSON shape",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        860,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const l = $('Clean text').item.json, o = $json.output;\nconst b = a => (a || []).map(x => '• ' + x).join('\\n');\nreturn { json: { Date: $now.setZone('Asia/Kolkata').toFormat('yyyy-LL-dd'), Company: l.company, Website: l.website, 'Fit score': o.fit_score, 'What they do': o.what_they_do,\n  Needs: b(o.likely_needs), Opener: o.opener,\n  email: `${l.company} (${l.website})\\nFit: ${o.fit_score}/10 – ${o.fit_reason}\\n\\nWHAT THEY DO\\n${o.what_they_do}\\n\\nWHO THEY SELL TO\\n${o.who_they_sell_to}\\n\\nSIZE\\n${o.size_signals}\\n\\n` +\n  `LIKELY NEEDS\\n${b(o.likely_needs)}\\n\\nTALKING POINTS\\n${b(o.talking_points)}\\n\\nOPENER\\n${o.opener}` } };",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      },
      "id": "04215f79-c091-4660-b3a3-dc71fd9e388d",
      "name": "Brief row",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1100,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const { email, ...row } = $json;\nreturn { json: row };",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      },
